servings: 1
---

In a #small bowl{}, whisk @egg yolks{6}.

In a #heavy bottom medium sized saucepan{}, add @sugar{1/2%cup}, @corn syrup{4%tbsp}, @salt{1/4%tsp}, and @Dutch process cocoa powder{1/2%cup}(optionally sifted). Whisk together to combine.

Set over medium heat, slowly whisking in @heavy cream{2%cups} and @milk{1%cup}, whisking constantly to combine everything.

Once the mixture is hot, take about 1 cup of the mixture and slowly incorporate it into the egg yolks, whisking constantly.

Once fully incorporated, slowly pour mixture back into the saucepan, again still whisking.

Cook, stirring constantly, until the mixture thickens. You do not want it to come to a boil, so watch carefully. When the mixture is thick enough to coat the back of a spoon it's done.

Immediately pour through a mesh sieve or cheesecloth into a bowl and stir in @vanilla{1%tsp}.

Cover and chill until cold. 

Churn your chilled mixture according to your machine's instructions (usually around 30 minutes).
 
For a soft-serve type experience, enjoy right away. Otherwise, freeze for at least 4 hours.